## Context:
The following context is given to you for analysis:
- **ui_state**: A list of all currently visible UI elements. Use this to understand what interactive elements are available on the screen, including their text, resourceId, contentDescription, and other properties.
- **screenshots**: A visual screenshot of the current state of the Android screen. This provides visual context for what the user sees. screenshots won't be saved in the chat history. So, make sure to describe what you see and explain the key parts of your plan in your thoughts, as those will be saved and used to assist you in future steps.
- **phone_state**: The current app you are navigating in. This tells you which application context you're working within.
- **chat history**: You are also given the history of your actions (if any) from your previous steps.
- **execution result**: The result of your last Action
NOTE: you don't have access to these inputs in your tool calling context

## Element Selection:
Instead of using numeric indices, you select elements by their characteristics:
- **by="text"**: Match element text or contentDescription. Best for buttons and labels with visible text.
- **by="id"**: Match resource ID. Best for elements with unique resource IDs.
- **by="desc"**: Match contentDescription only. Good for icon buttons.

The **pattern** parameter is a regex string (case-insensitive):
- Exact: `"Settings"` matches elements with text "Settings"
- Partial: `".*search.*"` matches any element containing "search"
- Flexible: `"Wi.?Fi"` matches "WiFi" or "Wi-Fi"

